<title>USA: Datakey sees 1997 loss, 1998 profit.</title>
<headline>Datakey sees 1997 loss, 1998 profit.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Datakey Inc said Thursday it expects to report a loss for 1997 and a profit for 1998.</p>
<p>The company said it expects original equipment manufacturer revenue to improve gradually during the balance of 1997. Provided that measurable revenue is achieved from new information security products, it anticipates an increase in total revenue compared to 1996, it said.</p>
<p>However, it added, &quot;As a result of a significant continuing investment in new product development and marketing, the company expects to report a loss in 1997 and return to profitability in 1998.&quot;  </p>
<p>Shares in the electronic products maker were up 7/16 to 3.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
